%% /run-issues — implementer timeout + auto-restart sequence
%% Companion to run-issues-state-machine.mmd. Shows the actors and ordering
%% across a first run that times out in S8 and the poller-driven restart that
%% follows. Update together with orchestrate.sh phase_b / restart_load_state,
%% lib/state.sh, and poller.sh scan_timed_out.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Poller as poller.sh (Studio LaunchAgent)
    participant Orch as orchestrate.sh
    participant Claude as claude-call.sh (timeout wrapper)
    participant State as run.json / state.jsonl
    participant GH as gh (Issues)

    Note over Poller,Orch: First run reaches S8_Implementer (auto mode)
    Orch->>State: enter_state S8_Implementer (current_state durable)
    Orch->>Claude: call_claude (timeout --kill-after=60 N)
    Claude--xClaude: claude overruns budget → SIGTERM (then SIGKILL +60s)
    Claude-->>Orch: rc=124 (subshell survives; .exit written)
    Orch->>State: finalize_timeout → status=timed_out,<br/>timeout_phase=S8_Implementer
    Orch-->>Poller: exit 7 (lock released, GitHub assignee kept)

    Note over Orch: Safety net — if a hard kill skipped the rc-handler,<br/>the EXIT trap re-reads run.json; non-terminal S8 → finalize_timeout

    Note over Poller: Next poll (≤5 min)
    Poller->>State: scan_timed_out (status=timed_out,<br/>retry_count<MAX, host==this)
    State-->>Poller: issue + run-dir
    Poller->>Orch: orchestrate.sh --restart <run-dir><br/>(tmux run-issues-restart-<N>)

    Orch->>State: validate status==timed_out, retry_count<MAX
    alt budget left and worktree OK
        Orch->>State: state_increment_retry (BEFORE claude call → durable spend)
        Orch->>Orch: ramp timeout = base*(1+retry), cap MAX
        Orch->>Orch: RESTART_CONTEXT = git log origin/main..HEAD
        Orch->>Claude: call_claude (longer budget, restart prompt)
        Claude-->>Orch: rc=0, IMPLEMENTER_RESULT: SUCCESS
        Orch->>State: continue S9..S12 → status=completed, PR opened
    else budget exhausted or worktree corrupt
        Orch->>State: finalize timed_out/blocked
        Orch->>GH: best-effort label needs-human + comment
        Orch-->>Poller: exit 0 (terminal; handed to human)
    end
